<title>UK: Sweden sets $50 million three-year bond.</title>
<headline>Sweden sets $50 million three-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Sumitomo Trust International and Toyo Securities Europe.</p>
<p> BORROWER   SWEDEN</p>
<p> AMT    $50 MLN	 COUPON     6.0	 MATURITY    30.MAY.00</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100	 PAY DATE  L-28.MAY.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.60	LISTING    NONE	PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  AA3/AA+   DENOMS (K) ONE	 SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> NOTES    L-LONG LAST COUPON</p>
<p>		ISSUED OFF THE EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
